## Before you start (the SessionStart hook would do this for you)
1. `git pull --ff-only` in the root{{MULTI_REPO_PULL_NOTE}}.
2. Read `{{COORDINATION_FILE}}` (open claims and messages only) and claim your item.
3. Read the `{{MEMORY_BANK_DIR}}/` of the repo you will work in (`repoMap.md`, `activeContext.md`).
4. `node scripts/md-size-watch.mjs --line` — act on a warning by archiving, never by deleting.

## Before you push (the push-guard hook would do this for you)
1. `node scripts/repomap-check.mjs <repo>` — new source files must be findable in `repoMap.md`.
2. The git pre-push hook (secret scan + syntax gate on deploy branches) is agent-independent and runs for you once `setup-hooks.sh` was executed.
3. Deploy branches: <!-- fill: list per repo, or "none". --> — pushing there is a deploy; confirm with the human first.

